if you're looking for a gift for an  architect in your life  don't be one of those people that get  some lego  what's going on guys my name is david  thomich and welcome back to the channel  today we're talking about some of the  best gifts that you can get for an  architect  in 2020 there is a million and one  things that you can get for somebody  i trolled the internet for a few hours  looking for some of the  best suggested architect gifts out there  and  99 of them are terrible from an  architect  to another potential architect watching  you probably know what i mean  there's people out there buying you  little lego blocks or  model bricks or concrete soap holders  all of these items are well and truly  good  but no architect really really wants  them  so if you're watching this looking to  buy a gift for an architect  today we're going to talk about 10  different products that might be perfect  for that person in your life so we're  going to start with  five tech related gifts that are very  specific to the niche of architecture  and the first one is of course a good  keyboard and mouse  if you know anything about what that  architect friend does all day  they more than likely sit at a computer  for 12 to 14 hours a day  just creating a way so this means that  they really want to be treated  and that extra couple hundred dollars  they spend on a keyboard and mouse combo  could be the difference between them  having couple tunnel and  major major risk problems in the future  to not at all  so this is my number one suggestion to  anybody looking to buy a gift for an  architect in 2020 moving on to the  second gift idea and it is the dji  om4 now this is the brand new gimbal  released by dji  i'll bring this one to your attention  today because architects  are having to create more and more  content in order to be able to promote  themselves as a personal brand  architects are being labeled as brands  now more so than anything  it isn't you go to a firm you go to a  very specific architect  so as architects we are creating more  and more for ourselves to be able to get  more and more clients for the firm  number three is one of my most used  tools  and something that i'm going to be  upgrading to very very shortly  it is the apple ipad pro with the apple  pencil  2. the reason i specify this product  here and  not any of the other ipads is for the  simple fact  of refresh rate screen brightness and  the compatibility with the pencil i  currently have an ipad air  it is the older generation i have to  have the old generation pencil  and the screen isn't very good whereas  at work we use the ipad pros the screen  resolution  is significantly better you can see the  details in the drawings and the  responsiveness of the pencil is much  much sharper  not to mention the fact that you can  easily snap it onto the side and charge  it  whilst you're talking during a meeting  whereas with the older generation you  have to stick it into the bottom  and you can't just pick it back up and  keep going it is a bit of an awkward  experience number four  if the lucky architect in your life  works at a rather large  practice with lots of people surrounding  them then  more than likely they're going to need  some good headphones to dry out the  noise  and pay attention to their work so  there's a number of options here  depending on the phone they use you can  either go with the apple air pods or you  can go with the sams and galaxy buds  alternatively  you can get a set of beats by dre that  are over the ear and cancel out the  noise extremely well  number five is the tech home gift for  all architects and creative tech nerds  it is philips hue lighting with a number  of different solutions  you can get them to just have fun at  home i personally purchased philips hue  lighting for my home it's in the bedroom  it's in the study here  and it's just a creative outlet  basically  now moving on to the next five products  they're all a little bit quirky  they're all a little bit interesting and  they all vary from very cheap to very  expensive  in the exact same category so i'm not  going to specify  anything for each individual product i'm  just going to give you a generic  recommendation here  they're all very useful for architects  and if you have an architect in your  life you're going to know why  pretty quickly so the first product of  choice is a 3d printer that's  potentially a laser cutter and a cnc  machine as well  the more we start to create and design  and the busier we get in life  the less time we have to physically  model at university architects have to  model  hundreds of different of little projects  and little homes out of cardboard and  styrofoam and wood  you genuinely just don't have time for  that in the real world  so a 3d printer becomes a great useful  tool  for any architect looking to model very  quickly and very rapidly  number two going back to my very first  point  and the simple fact that we work in a  chair and a desk for a very very long  period of time  so number two is a good ergonomic chair  and i think  anybody that sits down in an office for  a very long time can appreciate this  gift  number three personally speaking i do a  lot of travel as an architect i travel  five six hundred kilometers  every other week to visit my projects  and to visit my clients  so a good leather duffel bag is  extremely important  i personally don't have one but i find  that the more and more i travel  the better it would be to have something  that you could quickly pack  carry on and go now this is one of those  items that varies from relatively cheap  to very expensive  depending on your preference depending  on your style personally i think there's  a couple good options out there so  whatever you choose  i'm sure it will be a good choice number  four  is wireless security cameras for your  house they're very easy to install  they're tech related gift  which most architects will love because  we are all driven  by technology most of the time and yet  they are something that will keep us all  safe  and last but not least is again  something relating to  never being at home and never having too  much free time and that is a robot  vacuum  more so than not i'm having to find  myself quickly running around the house  cleaning it at the end of the week and i  just genuinely don't have that time for  it especially in the busy periods of  christmas  so having a robot vacuum would be a  greatly appreciated gift i'm sure  by any busy architect in 2020 anyway  that's all for me today guys thanks so  much for watching i hope you enjoyed the  video  i hope you got some useful information  out of it and some good gift ideas  if you did make sure you smash that like  button to help others with their gift  ideas  smash that subscribe button to see more  of my content and as always  i'll see you next monday

